---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy at Niyora"
  description="Niyora runs without an account and holds as little about you as it can. When you reflect, your words are stripped of identifying details before they are sent to an AI to write your reflection back."
  ogImage="https://assets.niyora.com/niyora-launch-poster.jpg"
  canonicalUrl="https://niyora.com/privacy/"
>
  <div class="container">
    <a class="back" href="/">← Back to Niyora</a>
    <p class="last-updated">Last updated: August 11, 2026</p>
    <h1>Privacy at Niyora</h1>

    <div class="promise">
      <p class="promise-text">Niyora runs without an account and holds as little about you as it can. Almost everything stays on your device. The one exception is the reflection itself, and we are plain about how that works.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>What stays on your device</h2>
    <p>Your period dates, session history, preferences, reminder schedule, and the notes you write live in the app on your phone. We run no account system, so there is no server profile of you to sign into, lose, or hand over. Your cycle data is used on your device to shape the app, and is never sent off it or shared.</p>

    <h2>How the reflection works</h2>
    <p>Moon's reflections are written by an AI model, which runs on a provider's servers rather than on your phone. So when you reflect on a moment, the words you write are sent to that provider to generate the response.</p>
    <p>Before anything is sent, your text is scrubbed on your device: names, places, and other identifying details are removed and replaced with neutral placeholders. The provider processes the scrubbed text to return a reflection. We do not attach an account or identity to it, because there is no account, and we keep no copy of it on a server of our own.</p>

    <h2>What we never do</h2>
    <p>No advertising identifiers. No cookies. No fingerprinting. No selling or sharing of your data. Your cycle data, in particular, is never sent off your device.</p>

    <h2>Optional, anonymous analytics</h2>
    <p>Only if you opt in, a small set of events (things like app launches and reminders firing) is sent to PostHog EU. Each event carries a random anonymous identifier generated only on opt-in, never tied to anything that identifies you, and never your reflections. You can turn it off any time in the app.</p>

    <h2>Questions?</h2>
    <p>Contact us at <a href="mailto:privacy@niyora.com">privacy@niyora.com</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  body { background: #0a0814; }
  .last-updated {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.35);
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .container {
    max-width: 640px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 60px 24px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7);
  }
  a.back {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.35);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 13px;
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }
  a.back:hover { color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6); }
  h1 {
    font-size: 28px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }
  .promise {
    margin-bottom: 48px;
    padding: 28px;
    background: rgba(20, 18, 32, 0.5);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
    border-radius: 12px;
  }
  .promise-text {
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.92);
    margin: 0;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8);
    margin: 32px 0 12px;
  }
  p, li {
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 300;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  ol {
    padding-left: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  ol li {
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  code {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
    padding: 1px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 13px;
  }
  a {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  a:hover {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1);
  }
</style>
